{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"0f1bf1ed-d028-4de3-a213-207d16e6aff3","step_index":10,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":2.618245,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"curl -sL \"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mpbXD3JUynFk6ws7nDvJ-BWATnE5MxE2PGEGZ1NMbOU/export?format=csv\""},"output":"1-PAGE MARKETING PLAN — DERIVOGRAFIA,,\r\r\n\"THE ITEM: A mobile app born at the biennale — visitors borrow an analog device for 1 hour, drift (dérive) and take one photograph; the app records the route and weaves it into a collective map in the exhibition room. Afterwards it lives on as a phone-only practice: one walk, one long-exposure image.\",,\r\r\nTHE SALE: Participation — every contributed walk on the collective map. Longer plays the plan quietly serves: traveling exhibitions \u0026 workshops (curators as a second audience) and premium app features later.,,\r\r\n,,\r\r\nBEFORE — THE PROSPECT (notice you),,\r\r\n\"1 · TARGET MARKET\r\n\r\nPrimary: the art-curious city walker (~20–45) who romanticizes analog — shoots film or wishes they did, is tired of 300 phone photos, follows slow-photography / psychogeography accounts, lives in or visits the biennale's city.\r\n\r\nSecondary: curators \u0026 cultural venues seeking participatory pieces that generate their own artwork.\",\"2 · MESSAGE\r\n\r\n\"\"One walk. One photograph.\"\" The anti-camera-roll: an hour of drifting condensed into a single image you cannot retake. Your walk doesn't disappear into your phone — it joins a living collective map, an artwork made of everyone's dérives.\r\n\r\nFor curators: \"\"an exhibition that grows itself — every visitor leaves a brushstroke.\"\"\",\"3 · MEDIA\r\n\r\nThe exhibition itself first: the loaned device, the wall map, QR codes.\r\n\r\nThen: Instagram / TikTok for the analog \u0026 slow-photography niche (walk → reveal videos), Lomography \u0026 film-photography communities, psychogeography / walking-art circles, local press + the biennale's own channels, art newsletters for the curator audience.\"\r\r\nDURING — THE LEAD (participate once),,\r\r\n\"4 · CAPTURE LEADS\r\n\r\nThe install IS the capture: to see your own route and receive the scan of your analog photo, you create an account (email). QR on the loaned device and beside the wall map.\r\n\r\nPost-show: a public web page with the live collective map and one action — \"\"add your walk.\"\"\",\"5 · NURTURE LEADS\r\n\r\nMonthly \"\"the map is growing\"\" email/post: new walks, one featured photo and its route. In-app gentle prompt after a quiet period. Instagram: the best single-photo walks (with permission).\r\n\r\nOccasional short essays on the dérive \u0026 slow photography — also the credibility file curators will read.\",\"6 · SALES CONVERSION\r\n\r\nGuided \"\"first dérive\"\" mode: the app deals a drift rule (\"\"follow anything red for 20 minutes\"\"), locks you to one exposure, runs the timer, reveals the image. Free, any phone, 20-minute starter — the full hour is the ritual. No bad photo when the rule is one.\r\n\r\nCurators: a \"\"bring derivografia to your city\"\" page with the aggregated map as proof.\"\r\r\nAFTER — THE CUSTOMER (become a fan),,\r\r\n\"7 · WORLD-CLASS EXPERIENCE\r\n\r\nTwo designed wow moments, systematized: (a) the delayed reveal — your developed analog photo arrives in the app days later, like a letter; (b) the post-walk reveal — the long exposure appears, then a small animation weaves YOUR route into the collective map.\r\n\r\nEverything should feel like receiving a postcard, not using an app.\",\"8 · LIFETIME VALUE\r\n\r\nMore walks per person: dérive series (\"\"night walks,\"\" \"\"one street for a month\"\"), seasonal collective projects, city chapters as the exhibition travels.\r\n\r\nLater, the premium layer: special exposure modes, printed postcards / books of your walks, paid workshops. Heavy contributors become ambassadors who host walks in their city.\",\"9 · REFERRALS\r\n\r\nAsk at the emotional peak — right after the photo reveal: \"\"send someone a drift rule\"\" (gift-a-dérive: your friend receives a rule, walks it, both routes appear side by side).\r\n\r\nEvery shared photo carries its route thumbnail and a \"\"walk your own\"\" link. At the show: visitors bring friends back to find their line on the wall map.\"\r\r\nA living document — revisit quarterly; change one square at a time rather than rewriting the plan.,,"}}}
