{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0f1bf1ed-d028-4de3-a213-207d16e6aff3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"# 1-Page Marketing Plan — Taller Lento\n\nYour complete 1-Page Marketing Plan has been created and saved in this directory:\n- [plan.csv](file:///private/tmp/mp-4OloRT/plan.csv) — The 3×3 grid ready for 1-click import into Google Sheets.\n- [plan.md](file:///private/tmp/mp-4OloRT/plan.md) — The comprehensive, readable strategy document with operational schedules and templates.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Pinned Assumptions (\"The Item\" \u0026 \"The Sale\")\n\nFollowing the guide's core rule, we define **the sale** before anything else. Mugs are what draw eyes at the fair, but wheel-throwing classes are what keep the studio alive:\n\n* **The Item:** An intimate wheel-throwing ceramics studio in Chacarita (**Taller Lento**, 6 wheels, 1 instructor) offering monthly 4-week courses and Saturday taster workshops, anchored by handmade stoneware mugs.\n* **The Sale (Conversion Definition):** A paid booking for the **monthly wheel-throwing course (ARS 120,000/mo)** or a taster class (ARS 40,000) that converts into the monthly course. The primary secondary conversion is **retention past Month 2** to fill both the Saturday morning (10:00–13:00) and new Wednesday evening (19:00–22:00) cohorts.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: The 3×3 Grid at a Glance\n\n| Phase | Square 1 | Square 2 | Square 3 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **BEFORE** *(Prospect)* | **1. Target Market**\u003cbr\u003eScreen-fatigued women (28–45) in Chacarita/Palermo/Colegiales; English-speaking expats \u0026 nomads. | **2. Message**\u003cbr\u003e*\"Tres horas sin pantallas. Barro en las manos, calma en la cabeza.\"* Intimate 6-wheel sanctuary with Lucía. | **3. Media**\u003cbr\u003ePalermo Sunday Fair booth; ASMR/process Instagram Reels; Google Maps listing; $40/mo local Meta ads. |\n| **DURING** *(Lead)* | **4. Capture Leads**\u003cbr\u003eTabletop QR stand at fair stall; direct `wa.me` in IG bio; WhatsApp Business triage tags. | **5. Nurture Leads**\u003cbr\u003e48-hour warm studio video follow-up; weekly IG Stories; monthly seat release broadcast. | **6. Sales Conversion**\u003cbr\u003eTaster class bridge with **50% fee roll-over credit** toward Month 1; instant WhatsApp Mercado Pago link. |\n| **AFTER** *(Customer)* | **7. World-Class Experience**\u003cbr\u003ePersonalized wheel welcome; same-night wheel photo sent via WhatsApp; kraft unboxing. | **8. Lifetime Value**\u003cbr\u003e3-month skill curriculum; Wednesday evening cohort (19:00–22:00); Week 3 priority re-enrollment. | **9. Referrals**\u003cbr\u003e\"Vení con un amigx\" 10% discount; organic story tagging; \"Regalá una clase\" vouchers at the fair. |\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Square-by-Square Breakdown\n\n#### 1. Target Market (*Who, exactly, this is for*)\n* **Primary:** Women aged 28–45 working high-screen, high-stress corporate, tech, or design jobs in Chacarita, Colegiales, Villa Crespo, and Palermo. They crave a grounding, offline, meditative ritual where their phones are stashed and their hands are in clay.\n* **Secondary:** English-speaking expats and digital nomads living in Buenos Aires seeking authentic, small-group creative classes taught in English.\n* **Tertiary (Top-of-funnel):** Design fair visitors looking for locally made gifts who are pottery-curious.\n\n#### 2. Message (*What makes them choose you*)\n* **Core Hook:** *\"Tres horas sin pantallas. Barro en las manos, calma en la cabeza.\"* (*Three hours offline. Clay in your hands, calm in your head.*)\n* **Differentiator:** Not an anonymous, crowded pottery factory with 20 students competing for equipment. An intimate 6-wheel garage sanctuary in Chacarita with individual attention from Lucía, your own wheel for the entire session, and high-fire stoneware you will actually use at home. English-friendly.\n\n#### 3. Media (*Where you reach them without wasting budget*)\n* **Palermo Sunday Fair:** Transform the existing ARS 35,000/week stall from just a mug counter into your primary offline student discovery engine.\n* **Instagram Reels (@taller.lento):** Process and ASMR videos (centering, trimming, glazing) already get 5–10× views. Post 1–2 per week with bilingual hooks.\n* **Google Business Profile (Maps):** Free setup for *\"Taller Lento — Clases de Cerámica y Torno en Chacarita\"*. Captures high-intent local searches like *\"clases de torno buenos aires\"*.\n* **Micro-Budget Ads ($40/mo):** Boost top-performing Reels to women aged 26–45 within a 3 km radius of Chacarita/Palermo, driving directly to WhatsApp.\n\n#### 4. Capture Leads (*Plugging the leaks*)\n* **The Fair Tabletop QR Stand:** Acrylic sign right next to the yerba mugs: *\"¿Querés aprender a tornear? Escaneá para info de clases y lista prioritaria.\"* Direct link to WhatsApp with a prefilled prompt (*\"Hola Lucía! Vi tus tazas en la feria y quiero info de clases\"*). Never say \"just follow my Instagram\" again.\n* **Instagram Bio:** Direct `wa.me` chat link, eliminating friction from the Linktree/PDF.\n* **WhatsApp Business:** Tag leads immediately: `[Interés Sábado]`, `[Interés Miércoles]`, `[Feria]`, `[Taster]`.\n\n#### 5. Nurture Leads (*Building trust before asking for money*)\n* **48-Hour WhatsApp Follow-up:** Send inquiring leads a warm 10-second studio video: *\"Quedan 2 tornos para el grupo de este mes. ¿Querés pasar a conocer o tenés alguna duda?\"*\n* **Instagram Stories Rhythm (3× a week, 5 mins each):** Unfiltered kiln openings, student smile moments, and remaining seat counts.\n* **Monthly Broadcast:** On the 20th of each month, message past inquiries when the next month's cohort seats open up.\n\n#### 6. Sales Conversion (*Removing risk and closing the sale*)\n* **The Two-Step Ladder:** Direct monthly enrollment (ARS 120,000) for ready students, and the Saturday taster (*\"Probá el torno\"*, ARS 40,000) for hesitant beginners.\n* **The 50% Roll-Over Credit:** If a taster student books the monthly class within 48 hours, **credit ARS 20,000 (50% of the taster fee) toward their first monthly payment**. This eliminates the taster drop-off.\n* **Frictionless Checkout:** Pre-written WhatsApp booking template with studio location pin, dates, and instant Mercado Pago / Transfer alias.\n\n#### 7. World-Class Experience (*Turning first-timers into fans*)\n* **Welcome Ritual:** Wheel prepared with the student's name on a small board, apron laid out, warm herbal tea in a signature yerba-green mug, and a guaranteed first centered piece in lesson 1.\n* **Same-Night Keepsake Photo:** Lucía snaps 2 candid, aesthetic photos of each student working the wheel with clay hands and sends them via WhatsApp that evening (primed for organic Instagram Story sharing).\n* **Unboxing Graduation:** Session 4 fired pieces presented wrapped in kraft paper, tied with jute twine, and accompanied by a handwritten note from Lucía.\n\n#### 8. Lifetime Value (*Ending the 1-month drop-off*)\n* **3-Month Skill Roadmap:** Replace the feeling of \"I made a bowl, I'm done\" with a progressive curriculum:\n  * *Month 1:* Centering, cylinders, bowls, and trimming.\n  * *Month 2:* Mug handles, pouring spouts, advanced glaze layering.\n  * *Month 3+:* Teapots, lidded vessels, and guided personal studio projects.\n* **Launch Wednesday Evening Group (19:00–22:00):** Captures students who drop Saturdays due to weekend travel; adds 4–6 recurring seats (ARS 480k–720k/mo).\n* **Week 3 Priority Re-enrollment:** Existing students get first right of refusal for their wheel for the next month before open spots go to the waitlist.\n\n#### 9. Referrals (*Systematic word-of-mouth*)\n* **\"Vení con un Amigx\":** Existing students and their friends both get **10% off their monthly fee** when signing up together (or a complimentary handmade mug).\n* **Organic Social Prompt:** With the session photos sent on WhatsApp: *\"Si lo compartís en stories, etiquetanos @taller.lento así lo resubimos!\"*\n* **Fair Gift Postcards:** *\"Regalá una experiencia de torno\"* vouchers at the Sunday fair stall — converts tourist and gift buyers into high-value workshop referrals.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: The 5-Hour Weekly Operating Rhythm\n\nFits entirely into Lucía's 5-hour marketing limit:\n\n| Day | Time | Action | Focus |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Sunday** | *0 hrs (during fair)* | Tabletop QR stand active beside mugs; converse with class inquiries. | Capture leads |\n| **Monday** | **1.0 hr** | Review WhatsApp tags, send 48-hour follow-up video messages. | Nurture \u0026 Convert |\n| **Wednesday** | **1.5 hrs** | Batch film \u0026 edit 1–2 wheel ASMR Reels during studio throwing time. | Media \u0026 Reach |\n| **Thursday** | **1.0 hr** | Post 3–4 Instagram Stories (kiln unboxing, student work, seat counts). | Nurture |\n| **Fri / Sat** | **1.5 hrs** | Send session photos to students; manage Week 3 re-enrollments. | Experience \u0026 Retention |\n| **Total** | **5.0 hrs/week** | | |\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: How to Import `plan.csv` into Google Sheets\n\n1. Open [Google Sheets](https://sheets.new) and create a blank sheet titled **\"1-Page Marketing Plan — Taller Lento\"**.\n2. Click **File → Import → Upload**, select [plan.csv](file:///private/tmp/mp-4OloRT/plan.csv), and choose **\"Replace current sheet\"**.\n3. **Format the 3×3 grid:**\n   * Select Columns **A, B, and C** and set their width to equal wide columns (**~390 pixels each**).\n   * Select the sheet and set **Text Wrapping to Wrap** and **Vertical Alignment to Top**.\n   * Set the three content rows (**Row 6, Row 8, Row 10**) to a fixed height of **~180–220 pixels**.\n   * Color the three phase band rows across columns A–C:\n     * **Row 5 (BEFORE):** Soft Sage Green (`#D9EAD3`), bold text.\n     * **Row 7 (DURING):** Soft Ochre / Amber (`#FCE5CD`), bold text.\n     * **Row 9 (AFTER):** Soft Terracotta / Rust (`#F4CCCC`), bold text.\n   * Freeze the top 4 rows via **View → Freeze → Up to row 4**.\n","duration_seconds":89.536122,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":100916,"output_tokens":21167,"thinking_tokens":11883,"cache_read_tokens":167055,"total_tokens":122083}}}
